th="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Paul III</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Paul III, born Alessandro Farnese, was pope from 1534 to 1549.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-iv"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-paul-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Paul IV</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Paul IV, born Gian Pietro Carafa, was pope from 1555 to 1559 and a leading figure of the Counter-Reformation.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Pius II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pius II, born Enea Silvio Piccolomini, was a humanist scholar and pope from 1458 to 1464.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-iv"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Pius IV</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pius IV (1499–1565), born Giovanni Angelo Medici in Milan, was pope from 1559 to 1565.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-ix"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-ix.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Pius IX</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pope Pius IX reigned from 1846 to 1878, the longest pontificate in history.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-v"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-v.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Pius V</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pope Pius V, a Dominican and former inquisitor, reigned from 1566 to 1572 and enforced the decrees of the Council of Trent.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-vi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Pius VI</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pius VI, born Giovanni Angelo Braschi, was pope from 1775 to 1799.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-vii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Pius VII</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pius VII, born Barnaba Chiaramonti, was pope from 1800 to 1823.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-xi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-xi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Pius XI</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pope Pius XI, born Achille Ratti, was pope from 1922 to 1939.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-siricius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-siricius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Siricius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Siricius was bishop of Rome from 384 to 399.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-sixtus-iv"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-sixtus-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Sixtus IV</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pope Sixtus IV reigned from 1471 to 1484.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-sixtus-v"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-sixtus-v.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Sixtus V</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sixtus V was pope from 1585 to 1590.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-stephen-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-stephen-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Stephen II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pope Stephen II reigned from 752 to 757.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-sylvester-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-sylvester-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Sylvester II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pope Sylvester II, born Gerbert of Aurillac, was a French scholar who became the first French pope, reigning from 999 to 1003.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-urban-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Urban II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pope Urban II was bishop of Rome from 1088 to 1099.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-iv"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-urban-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pope Urban IV</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pope Urban IV, born Jacques Pantaléon in Troyes, was pope from 1261 to 1264, a former archdeacon of Liège and patriarch of Jerusalem.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-viii"><img class="enc-